        "original_id": "93f44868-d65b-5f89-921a-83b743891db0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tony Hendra, Stephen Hawking, John Cleese, Graham Chapman, Tim Brooke-Taylor\n- Organizations: St Albans School, Cambridge University, Cambridge University Footlights, Centre for Theoretical Cosmology, University of Cambridge\n- Products: National Lampoon The Iron On Book\n- Roles: satirist, actor, writer, theoretical physicist, cosmologist, author, Director of Research\n\nFacts:\n- Tony Hendra was born on 10 July 1941 and is an English satirist, actor, and writer who has worked mostly in the United States.\n- In 1962, Tony Hendra was a member of the Cambridge University Footlights revue alongside John Cleese, Graham Chapman, and Tim Brooke-Taylor.\n- Tony Hendra was educated at St Albans School, where Stephen Hawking was his classmate, and at Cambridge University.\n- Stephen Hawking was born on 8 January 1942 and is an English theoretical physicist, cosmologist, author, and Director of Research at the Centre for Theoretical Cosmology within the University of Cambridge.\n- Tony Hendra edited National Lampoon The Iron On Book.",
